    "turn_text": "I did play up there. And in fact, the year that I was there, the Jayhawks, from neighboring Kansas that won the National Beach Civil and National Championship, the National Basketball Championship, which was, you know, a little hard to take being being a Missouri boy, but they came to the reason I mentioned is the Chief Justice, who's also a big sports fan, the Chief Justice invited them to come to the Supreme Court when they made their DC trip, and they got invited to the White House. Chief Justice said, well, why don't you come to the Supreme Court? And they had the truly master stroke idea. He said, let's invite them to do a scrimmage. You shoot around at the highest court in the land, which they did. So it was kind of awesome. Even though it was Kansas, it was kind of awesome to see those guys up at the highest court in the land up there shooting around. And you know, we got this. go out there with them and then we had them for lunch and all that stuff. But yeah, the clerks would get together and play from time to time. I'll be honest with you, basketball is not my sport, but it's, you know, it's awesome to be up there and to be able to think about, you know, this is a court that not only have the justices played on over the years. Michael Jordan has played on that court. Clarence Thomas uh, was friends with Jordan. I think still is and invited him to come. And so he's, he shot around on that court and, you know, so that's pretty",
