    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81053.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 72,
    "turn_text": "Okay, so this grew the the intersection of sports in China, some people who have not followed this case closely, but are listening to us now back in October, the NBA, which has had a very deep relationship with China as they've expanded their brand around the world. The NBA was on sort of a goodwill tour around Asia. and the Houston rocket GM, Daryl Moray tweeted free Hong Kong as a part of the Hong Kong protests. And all hell basically broke loose in terms of the NBA's relationship with China. And before I get into the specifics of that, you actually traveled over to China to witness the Hong Kong protest for yourself. I understand back in October of last year, And we've certainly seen this relationship devolve. I mean, in fact, all of the protesters and what they were protesting for has been proven to be 100% true, maybe even stunning to me, maybe to you as well, how quickly China has moved to curtail those basic human rights and freedoms in Hong Kong. But what did you see on your trip in October as these protests were going on?",
