    "turn_text": "mean, the NBA's, what's their latest contract just this past year worth over $1.5 billion. I mean, it's just unbelievable the amount of money. You mentioned the, you know, sort of the woke stance that the India is taking, it's corporate, it's classic corporate wokeness. It's nothing that would interfere with profits for heaven's sake. I mean, profit, oh my gosh, we're going to get those. And nothing that would interfere with our multinational plan to scoop up money in all of these different markets and for so many American corporations, if that means selling out the American worker, sending jobs overseas, oh, by God, we'll do that in a heartbeat. But don't get mad at us because we're woke. It's really a huge distraction to try and move attention away from what they're really doing, what these huge corporations are really doing. And the MBA is right there in terms of the money they are making in China and the kind of deal that they have made with the Chinese government. And I think it is not too much to ask them, which is my point of silver in my letter. Well, first of all, what is the deal with China? Why aren't you saying anything as you make all this money as an organization? And at the very least, if you're going to put statements on the back of jerseys,",
